    "statement": "NOT STATIONARY AND NOT STABLE, and the movement is not the denominator's. Pooled over 8-min frames the winner's NORMALIZED position has sd 1.466 decades against sd 0.742 decades for the local median, so the position on the shape moves about twice as much as the normalization denominator does. The normalized term accounts for 136% of the variance of the absolute boundary and the cross term is -71% \u2014 the two partly cancel, which is why the absolute track looks calmer than either component. Consecutive frames overlap by 7/8 of their window, yet the winner moves by more than 0.5 decades between 27.3% of adjacent frame pairs and by more than 1.0 decade between 17.5%. A boundary that relocates by a factor of ten between two windows sharing 87.5% of their data is not tracking a slowly-moving shape; it is switching between candidates. Chart 03 shows why there are candidates to switch between.",
